Objective completion before activation: many missions report an objective
accomplished or failed (Set_Objective_Status) before the script that adds it
has run, because the add is gated on a conversation end or a zone (M02
202/203/213/217, M03 1002/1004/1007/1008, M06 601/603/609, M07 703-708/710).
The status call found no objective and did nothing, and the later
Add_Objective left the objective pending for the rest of the mission on the
HUD, the EVA objectives tab and the score screen.

Remember the latest terminal status (accomplished/failed) of each unknown ID
in a bounded file-local table (32 entries, oldest evicted, cleared by Reset).
When Add_Objective creates that ID as pending, replay the status through the
original Set_Objective_Status path. A pending/hidden report for an unknown ID,
Remove_Objective, or any add of the ID consumes the entry. A replay marker
absorbs one same-status repeat before the next Update, so scripts that credit
a late add themselves (scripts-a38-m03-*-late-add, M04 torpedo race) do not
announce the completion twice. Objectives added before their status change
never touch the table.

Save compatibility: pending entries are written as new micro-chunk 2
({ID, Status}, 8 bytes each) inside the existing manager-variables chunk.
Older loaders ignore unknown micro-chunks; older saves have none and load
with an empty table. Replay markers are not saved.

See reports/campaign/OBJECTIVE_EARLY_STATUS.md.

